  "preamble": "Coronalization of the bilabial stop [p] to [t]. In attested cases this is regressive assimilation in a stop cluster, *pt > tt, where the labial takes on the place of the following dental. It happened throughout Middle Indo-Aryan (Sanskrit sapta > Pali and Prakrit satta) and in central and southern Italo-Romance (Latin septem > Italian sette).",
